  ...SPEAK('MK5', 'Speaking, Pitch a product in one minute',
    'You are a sales assistant at Green Leaf Tea. A shop owner in District 7 is thinking of selling one of your products. Pitch ONE product (cold brew, oolong tea, a gift box or tea biscuits) for about 1 minute.\n• Open with a hook and introduce the product.\n• Compare it with at least one other product (use comparatives or superlatives).\n• Give the price and where it is sold, and end with a clear request.',
    `Good morning, Mr Phuc. Do your customers want a healthy snack with their tea? Let me introduce our mango tea biscuits from Green Leaf Tea. They are made with Da Lat green tea and real mango, so they are lighter and less sweet than normal biscuits. In our own shops, they are the most popular snack with students. A pack of eight costs 35,000 VND, which is cheaper than most imported biscuits. We deliver every Monday, and the smallest order is only twenty packs. Why don't you try one box this month? If your customers don't like them, we will take them back.`,
    'Content: opens with a hook, introduces one product, makes at least two comparisons, gives price and place, and ends with a clear request'),
  ...WRITE('MK5', 'Writing, A product pitch email',
    'You are Linh, marketing assistant at Green Leaf Tea. Write an email of about 120 words to Ms Tran Thi Hoa, the owner of Hoa Coffee, a group of cafes near the universities in Thu Duc. Purpose: persuade her to sell Green Leaf oolong tea in her cafes.\n• Introduce the product and say why it suits students.\n• Compare it with one other drink (use comparatives or superlatives).\n• Give the price and suggest a next step (for example a free tasting or a trial order).',
    `Dear Ms Hoa,\n\nI am writing to introduce Green Leaf oolong tea, grown on a family farm in Bao Loc.\n\nMany students in Thu Duc study late and want a drink that keeps them awake. Our oolong is lighter than coffee and has less caffeine, so students can enjoy it in the evening and still sleep well. It is also the most popular hot tea in our own shops.\n\nA 500-gram bag costs 220,000 VND and makes about 120 cups, so it is cheaper per cup than most milk tea.\n\nWould you like us to hold a free tasting in one of your cafes next week? After that, you could try a small order of ten bags.\n\nI look forward to hearing from you.\n\nBest regards,\nLinh\nGreen Leaf Tea`,
    'Content: introduces the product with a reason it suits students, makes at least one clear comparison, and gives the price and a next step', 120),

